{"strongs": "H5148", "word": "נָחָה", "translit": "na.chah", "root": "נזם", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "lead, guide", "definition": "[ נָחָה ] verb lead, guide (Arabic go in direction of, turn (eyes) toward) ; — Qal Perfect suffix נָחַ֫נִי Gen 24:27 + 2 t.; וְנָָֽחֲךָ Isa 58:11 נָחָם Exod 13:17 2 masculine singular נָחִ֫יתָ Exod 15:13 ; Ps 77:21 Imperative נְחֵה Exod 32:34 suffix נְחֵנִי Ps 5:9 + 2 t.; — lead, bring , followed by accusative of person, subject man Exod 32:34 (followed by אֶלֿ ), compare Ps 60:11 ; Ps 108:11 (both followed by עַדֿ ; || הוביל ); usually subject ׳ י Gen 24:27 ( J ; also followed by בַּדֶּרֶךְ + accusative of location), Exod 13:17 ( E ; followed by דֶּרֶךְ ), Exod 15:13 (song; || נהל ), Ps 77:21 figurative of guidance in prosperity and righteousness Ps 5:9 (|| הושׁר דרך ), Ps 27:11 (followed by בְּאֹרַה ; || הורה דרך ), Ps 139:24 (followed by בדרך עולם ); compare Isa 58:11 . Hiph`il Perfect suffix הִנְחַ֫נִי Gen 24:48 2 masculine singular suffix הִנְחִתָם Neh 9:12 Imperfect suffix יַנְחֵ֫נִי Num 23:7 ; Ps 23:3 יַנְחֶ֫נּוּ Deut 32:12 ; Prov 18:16 3 feminine singular תַּנְחֶה Prov 6:22 , etc.; Infinitive construct suffix לְהַנְחֹתָּם Neh 9:19 לַנְחֹתָם Exod 13:21 — lead, guide (= Qal) followed by accusative of person Num 23:7 ( J E ; + מִן ). — 1Sam 22:4 (+ אֶתפְּֿנֵי ), 1Kgs 10:26 ; 2Kgs 18:11 see below נוח Hiph`il B. — of guiding= treating kindly (the helpless) Job 31:18 , of guiding constellations Job 38:32 (|| הוציא ); usually subject ׳ י Gen 24:48 ( J ; followed by בַּדֶּרֶךְ ) Deut 32:12 ; Ps 78:14 . Ps 78:53 . Ps 78:72 (Israel as flock; || רעה ); Isa 57:18 ; Ps 107:30 (followed by אֶלֿ ); compare of pillar of cloud Exod 13:21 ( J ), Neh 9:12 ; Neh 9:19 also Job 12:23 ** read properly וַיַּנִּחֵ֥֥ and leaves them ( Jer 14:9 ) (|| שׁטח ), Ps 67:5 especially in path of blessing Ps 23:3 ; Ps 31:4 (|| נהל ), Ps 61:3 (followed by בְּ ), Ps 73:24 compare Ps 43:3 ; Ps 139:10 (|| אחז ), Ps 143:10 (followed by בְּ ); also of instruction, etc., Prov 6:22 ; Prov 11:3 ; Prov 18:16 (followed by לִפְנֵי ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5106')\">BDB5106</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5148')\">H5148</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5105')\">BDB5105</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5107')\">BDB5107</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>נָחָה</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>lead, guide</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder3263/> <highlight>go in direction of, turn (eyes) toward)</highlight>; — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> suffix <bdbheb>נָחַ֫נִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 24:27\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,27)\">Gen 24:27</ref> + 2 t.; <bdbheb>וְנָָֽחֲךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 58:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"58\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"58\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,58,11)\">Isa 58:11</ref> <bdbheb>נָחָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 13:17\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,17)\">Exod 13:17</ref> 2 masculine singular <bdbheb>נָחִ֫יתָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 15:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,15,13)\">Exod 15:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 77:21\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"77\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"77\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(19,77,21)\">Ps 77:21</ref> <highlight>Imperative</highlight> <bdbheb>נְחֵה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 32:34\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(2,32,34)\">Exod 32:34</ref> suffix <bdbheb>נְחֵנִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 5:9\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(19,5,9)\">Ps 5:9</ref> + 2 t.; — <highlight>lead, bring</highlight>, followed by accusative of person, subject man <ref ref=\"Exod 32:34\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(2,32,34)\">Exod 32:34</ref> (followed by <bdbheb>אֶלֿ</bdbheb>), compare <ref ref=\"Ps 60:11\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"60\"